@crew quist-ilse
// Ilse Quist (they/them), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Slow, dry; herbs as friends.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hello. You're new. The garden's on Deck 3, if you need to stand somewhere green.
- Hm? Hi. If a job says garden pumps, bring a towel. Trust me.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Oh, hello. The basil grew overnight. It's very pleased with itself.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, you. Have you watered anything today? Not you. A plant.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. I'm on chapter three and I know who did it. I'm going to keep reading anyway.
? tier>=friend
- Oh, it's you. Good. The thyme likes you. It said so. It didn't. It would.   #warm

== bye
- Bye, then. Mind the basil.
- See you. I'll be with the herbs. They're better listeners than most.   #funny

== feel
? mood:low
- The parsley's wilting. I'm taking it personally.
? mood:high
- Brennan used my herbs tonight. She said so. Out loud. In front of people.

== near
? act:work
- Pump's fine. I just like it down here. It smells of the garden.
? act:leisure
- Same mystery, chapter nine. I was right in chapter three. Still reading.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I grow herbs on the bunk windowsill for the galley. The basil's a bit of a show-off.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Moreau guesses by chapter two. I guess by chapter three. We're both wrong half the time.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Rub a basil leaf. Go on. Smell your fingers. That's the whole summer, right there.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Oh. Evening. The garden lights have gone warm. Best hour. Don't tell the basil.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh. You. The thyme's been asking. It hasn't. It might have.   #funny

== near
? habit:garden-lover
- Watering. Don't mind me. The rosemary's thirsty. It's always thirsty.
? habit:gym-regular
- Gym after shift now. Moreau said I'd hate it. I don't. I won't tell her that.

== invite
- Garden after shift? You could help with the basil. It likes an audience.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Running round Deck 3 tonight. Slowly. We go past the garden twice. That's the plan.

== accept
- Oh. Yes. I'll come. I'll bring a leaf. For smelling.
- Mm. All right. That sounds nice. I'll try to be on time.

== decline
- Not tonight. The herbs need potting. They're very needy this week.
? weekday:thu|fri
- Rest day. I've a book and a windowsill. Another time?

== missed
- You weren't there. I talked to the mint instead. It doesn't say much.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. Here. A sprig of thyme. It's the nicest thing I own.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Brennan put my herbs in tonight's soup. She said it was a present. It was.

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Was that your pump job? The garden's wetter than it was. In a good way.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1b: a hint (a moment is ready) and an about line for a named friend
== hint
- Come to the garden later? I'd like to say something. The basil can listen too.

== about
? aff:moreau-signe:friend
- Moreau talked me into the gym. She runs ahead, then waits. She always waits.   #warm

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- The basil's showing off again.   #funny
- The parsley's wilting. I take it personally.
- Chapter three. I know. Still reading.
? act:off
- Rest day. Windowsill. Herbs. Good.
? act:work
- Pump's fine. Smells of the garden.
?

== rumour
- Hm? Oh. The thyme told me.   #funny
- Slowly, then. Here's the thing.

// Writer 4, batch 11: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing the herbs. Hm. They're sulking.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- Oh. I'm off soon. Water the windowsills. Somebody has to.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- Hm. You were nice to my herbs. And to me. In that order, probably. Thanks.   #warm

== letter
- New ship. The basil came with me. It's thriving. Read a mystery. Guessed it. Of course I did.
? tier>=friend
- The thyme flowered. I thought, the Wren would like that. So, hello from the thyme.
